3. SCORABLE ROWS — and the TWO nan conditions, counted separately
   `fi` is nan when D_est is empty. `iou` is nan only when the UNION is empty,
   i.e. D_est AND D_true both empty. F2a treated them as one condition; they are not,
   and the margin over IoU is much smaller than the margin over fi.
